{"Implementation approach":"Bob (Architect) proposes a small, acyclic Python 3.10 package that cleanly separates concerns: foundational errors and history; a tokenizer that is the sole owner of token classes and scans input deterministically; a pure engine implementing shunting-yard and RPN evaluation; a thin API that composes tokenizer and engine and integrates History; a thin entrypoint. Preserve protocol files exactly (requirements.txt, Main.py, tests/test_main.py). Keep runtime entry minimal and headless. Use only standard library plus pytest in requirements. Adhere strictly to import direction errors/history -> tokenizer -> engine -> api -> __init__/Main/tests. Enforce tokenizer ownership: only Token, NumberToken, OpToken, LParenToken, RParenToken, and Tokenizer are defined in calculator/tokenizer.py, with the only project import being 'from .errors import TokenizationError'. Ensure engine.py literally imports tokens via 'from .tokenizer import Token, NumberToken, OpToken, LParenToken, RParenToken'. Avoid Python 3.11+ APIs. Ensure every scanning branch advances or raises. Evaluate rejects blank input with ParseError and appends exactly one History record on success. Tests are deterministic, concise, and rely only on the canonical public API and run_demo. Each file stays under ~150 LOC.","Domain Decomposition":[["Build/test dependency declaration","requirements.txt","protocol-required"],["Error hierarchy (foundation)","calculator/errors.py","package"],["Immutable calculation history (append-only; returns copies)","calculator/history.py","package"],["Token types (sole ownership) and deterministic tokenizer with unary sign folding","calculator/tokenizer.py","package"],["Shunting-yard to RPN and RPN evaluation with clear parse/eval errors","calculator/engine.py","pure-rule"],["Public API: evaluate and tokenize; History integration and input validation","calculator/api.py","interface"],["Canonical public exports (__all__)","calculator/__init__.py","package"],["Thin runtime entry with non-interactive demo","Main.py","environment-dependent"],["Protocol-level concise tests (exactly three) using only public API and run_demo","tests/test_main.py","automated-test"]],"File list":["requirements.txt","calculator/errors.py","calculator/history.py","calculator/tokenizer.py","calculator/engine.py","calculator/api.py","calculator/__init__.py","Main.py","tests/test_main.py"],"Canonical File References":["requirements.txt","calculator/errors.py","calculator/history.py","calculator/tokenizer.py","calculator/engine.py","calculator/api.py","calculator/__init__.py","Main.py","tests/test_main.py"],"Data structures and interfaces":"classDiagram
