    API-->>M: result(float)
    T->>M: run_demo()
    M-->>T: {"expression": str, "result": float, "history_len": int}","Domain Mapping":[["calculator/errors.py defines foundational exceptions","calculator/errors.py","Defines CalculatorError (base), TokenizationError, ParseError, EvaluationError; no external imports needed other than builtins; no dependencies on other project modules."],["calculator/history.py immutable, append-only history","calculator/history.py","History maintains an internal list of (expression, result). add appends; records returns a shallow copy; __len__ returns count. No imports from other project modules."],["calculator/tokenizer.py sole owner of token classes and tokenizer","calculator/tokenizer.py","Defines Token (marker), NumberToken(frozen, value: float), OpToken(frozen, op: str), LParenToken(), RParenToken(). Tokenizer.tokenize(expression: str)->list[Token] ignores whitespace, recognizes numbers (integers/decimals), operators + - * /, parentheses. Unary + or - at start or after operator or '(' must fold into the following number; malformed numbers and invalid characters raise TokenizationError. Every branch advances index or raises to avoid stalls. Only project import: from .errors import TokenizationError. The forbidden strings 'from .tokenizer import' and 'from calculator.tokenizer import' must not appear."],["calculator/engine.py parsing and evaluation","calculator/engine.py","Literally imports: from .tokenizer import Token, NumberToken, OpToken, LParenToken, RParenToken. Imports ParseError and EvaluationError from .errors. Implements to_rpn(tokens:list[Token])->list[Token] using shunting-yard with precedence (* and / > + and -) and parentheses, raising ParseError for malformed expressions (e.g., mismatched parentheses, operator misuse). Implements eval_rpn(rpn:list[Token])->float using a float stack; performs operations; raises EvaluationError for division by zero and stack errors."],["calculator/api.py public API composition","calculator/api.py","Imports Tokenizer, Token from .tokenizer; to_rpn, eval_rpn from .engine; History from .history; ParseError from .errors. tokenize(expression) thinly delegates to Tokenizer().tokenize. evaluate(expression, history=None): rejects blank/whitespace-only with ParseError; tokenizes; to_rpn; eval_rpn; on success, if history provided, appends exactly one record; propagates TokenizationError, ParseError, EvaluationError unchanged; returns float."],["calculator/__init__.py public re-exports","calculator/__init__.py","Explicitly re-exports evaluate, tokenize from .api; History from .history; CalculatorError, TokenizationError, ParseError, EvaluationError from .errors. No extra aliases."],["Main.py thin runtime entry","Main.py","Uses 'from calculator import evaluate, History'. Defines run_demo()->dict: evaluates one fixed expression using a History, returns a dict with expression, result, history_len. Under __name__ guard, prints one concise value (e.g., result) and exits. No input loops, no network/FS/time."],["tests/test_main.py concise protocol-level tests","tests/test_main.py","Exactly three pytest tests using only 'from calculator import evaluate, tokenize, History, CalculatorError, TokenizationError, ParseError, EvaluationError' and 'from Main import run_demo'. Tests: (1) run_demo returns a dict and evaluate('2 + 3 * 4') == 14.0; (2) a single History records exactly ('(1 + 2) * 3', 9.0) and len(tokenize('1 + 2.5')) == 3; (3) division by zero raises EvaluationError, evaluate('1 @ 2') raises TokenizationError, and blank input raises ParseError. No token construction, isinstance checks, reflection, or internal-module imports."]],"Testable Core Boundary":{"pure_logic_modules":["calculator/errors.py","calculator/history.py","calculator/tokenizer.py","calculator/engine.py","calculator/api.py","calculator/__init__.py"],"environment_dependent_modules":["Main.py"],"test_targets_should_focus_on":["Basic runtime wiring via run_demo() returning a dict","Operator precedence: '*' and '/' over '+' and '-'","Tokenization count for '1 + 2.5' equals 3 without introspection","Error pathways: blank ParseError, invalid char TokenizationError, division-by-zero EvaluationError","History records exactly one entry on successful evaluation"]},"C++ Interface Plan":{},"Test Include Audit":{"declared_test_imports":["from calculator import evaluate, tokenize, History, CalculatorError, TokenizationError, ParseError, EvaluationError","from Main import run_demo"],"undeclared_test_includes":[],"all_test_includes_declared":true},"Protocol Compliance Check":{"build_file_preserved":true,"runtime_entry_preserved":true,"test_target_preserved":true,"test_command":"python -m pytest -q","required_files_missing":[],"required_files_renamed":[],"unexpected_additional_test_files":[],"noncanonical_file_references":[],"canonical_matches_file_list":true,"canonical_missing_from_file_list_copy":[],"canonical_extra_paths":[],"protocol_violations":[]},"Protocol Preservation Notes":"Build file: requirements.txt. Runtime entry: Main.py. Single test target: tests/test_main.py. Test command: python -m pytest -q. Exactly one protocol-level test file is used.","Anything UNCLEAR":""}

